BTW, I've decided I like daggers as much if not more than runed daggers in
the long run, once you have enough resource to acquire multiple blessed
enchant weapon scrolls.

Here's why.  I like having about 20-24 enchanted daggers, and carry 12-16 to
fight, and have reserve in my stash/BagoHolding.  Reserve is there for when
the enchanted daggers get eaten by rust monsters/disenchanters, or lost in
the water or lava or something.

Now, It's definitely possibly to collect that much runed daggers.  However,
most of the time, you get twice, maybe three times that amount of daggers.

That means you can try to over-enchant daggers above +7.  You simply split
the entire stock of 50 some +7 daggers in half, and attempt to enchant that
24+ daggers to +8.  If it succeed, the daggers are obviously now better than
+7 runed daggers.  If it fails, you still end up with 24+ some +7 daggers
which are still really good and functionally there's really not much
difference between +7 daggers and +7 runed daggers.  If you succeed on the
first pile, you can try it on the second pile and see if you can come up
with 50some +8 daggers.  Now you can go for +9.  And so on.

You get soooo many daggers that this is usually the case, while you almost
never get enough runed daggers.  It's just a pain looking for runed daggers.

